{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 13, :comments ["<b>I settled.</b> From a gezerah shavah (Esther 5:13), and the word 'my soul' is missing. The correct interpretation is that it refers to the illness, for it is equal in the strength of its battle against me like a lion, and the habit of the lion is to shatter the bones, and the wonder is that at night it battles me and makes peace for me in the morning:"], :book :isaiah, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 38, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Isaiah, by M. Friedlander; Society of Hebrew Literature, London 1877" "https://www.nli.org.il/he/books/NNL_ALEPH001338443"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T18:56:51.637665847Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}